                    {
                        "name":  "places/ChIJ0cV-48OrQjQRnS93QuZM59k/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21GeU0ybHRWSFpoT1hGd1kyMURlVE54U1daclVtYxAB",
                        "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "5 months ago",
                        "rating":  4,
                        "text":  {
                                     "text":  "The place feels too pretentious for what it seems to self-identify as. The pizza itself is not terrible (don’t get the salami one if you hate overly salty food though). One pizza is plenty for two semi-hungry people and they can even make the pizza half and half. However, getting a full pizza and a drink is not enough to get over the fine print minimum order amount per person so the staff made us order more things we did not actually want. Maybe that’s specifics of Taiwan market.",
                                     "languageCode":  "en"
                                 },
                        "originalText":  {
